{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270588",
      "title": "More Reasons For Why Keys Matter",
      "sourceHash": "09c05180328b7c5aef09fc8bc13ffbd070a6f490353678a440df9974837a8358",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.87,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "Now adding such a key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "also has another benefit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "besides making sure that the state doesn't jump around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "And to show you this benefit, I'll temporarily go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "to using such a index, which of course is a bad solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 16.743,
          "en": "as you saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 20.31,
          "en": "Because when I do that and I reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.31,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "and I now go to the Elements tab and I inspect this list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "please watch this list here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 28.77,
          "en": "and the list items here on the right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.77,
          "end": 30.693,
          "en": "as I click those buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "You'll notice that every time I click a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 37.8,
          "en": "basically all list items change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 41.73,
          "en": "They all flash, which means they all change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.73,
          "end": 43.983,
          "en": "they're all touched by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 47.64,
          "en": "And that happens because at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "I'm using index as a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "and therefore when I click Increment here for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 55.71,
          "en": "and React creates these DOM snapshots,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.71,
          "end": 58.92,
          "en": "it sees that in the end it now has a totally different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "HTML code that should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "because a new item was added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "And it therefore basically throws away the old list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.643,
          "en": "and re-renders the new list because everything changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "Now of course, to us humans it's clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 77.19,
          "en": "that that's not really the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 80.7,
          "en": "Instead, it's only the first list item that was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.7,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "when we click such a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "and the other items are just the old items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "moved down by one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "But because we're using this index key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 91.623,
          "en": "React doesn't know that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now, if we switch to that better key of count ID here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.12299999999999,
          "en": "you'll see that this changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 105.06,
          "en": "If I save this and reload and inspect that list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.06,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "and you again watch that list here on the right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "you'll see that as I change it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 115.781,
          "en": "it's now only parts of the list that are updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.781,
          "end": 120.781,
          "en": "and the other elements are not updated, are not flashing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "Instead it's really just the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "that is updated here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 127.8,
          "en": "If you see the second element flashing as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.8,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "that's really just because I'm sometimes clicking too fast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 134.25,
          "en": "It's just the first element that's being updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.25,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "because React does indeed now understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "that the other elements were part of the DOM before as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "because it knows that key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.77,
          "en": "from the previous virtual DOM snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.77,
          "end": 149.01,
          "en": "because that key is also stored there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.01,
          "end": 153.12,
          "en": "And it's therefore able to reuse those old DOM elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.12,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "and instead of recreating them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "it just inserts a new element in front of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "And therefore, using such a key does not just help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "with state management, as shown in the previous lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 170.85,
          "en": "Instead, it also helps React render such lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.85,
          "end": 172.173,
          "en": "in a more optimal way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}